From: Nguyen Phan <nguyen@nguyenphan.org>
Date: Mon, 10 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41: publish the replicated pool's rows

With KV sharding off (KV_SHARD=0) the pool is replicated on every rank, so the shard's per-part
counters (kv_parts) have nothing to report and the pool's occupancy was not published at all: the
common case had no numbers. A backend now hands the host a pool Source (core/lanes/pool.zig,
family-neutral), read on the engine thread at each noteLive and published for status readers.

/metrics: kv_pool_rows, kv_pool_live, kv_pool_kept, kv_pool_free, kv_pool_streams; the status carries
the same numbers under pool. A backend that publishes no pool shows nothing, as before.
